  "placement": "Book pages 84–86, topic 3.8: নিউটনের তৃতীয় গতি সূত্র (Newton's Third Law of Motion). Next to the boxed law, the action–reaction paragraph and চিত্র ৩.১২ (an apple and the Earth pulling each other).",
  "order": 1,
  "maintainers": ["RadeenXALNW"],
  "units": "m",
  "description": "Newton's third law (Physics 9–10, topic 3.8, pp84–86): a boy jumps from a wooden boat onto a jetty while the boat recoils. Equal, opposite horizontal contact forces act on two different bodies only while his feet push on the boat; after takeoff, separate velocity arrows show the motion. The apple–Earth example shows the complete NASA Blue Marble globe, a red apple, equal and opposite gravitational forces, centre-to-centre distance R and the textbook equations F = GmM/R² = mg, a_m = g and a_M = F/M = (m/M)g ≈ 1.64×10^-24 m/s² for m = 1 kg and M = 5.98×10^24 kg. Sizes and separation are explicitly not to scale. Five tap questions connect the pictures to the force-pair principle. Offline, Bangla/English, with self-contained GLB exports. Version 1.0 replaces the equal/unequal skater example IDs with boat; apple remains apple.",
  "tags": ["force", "newtons-laws", "action-reaction", "third-law", "acceleration", "bangla"],
